  "methods_or_SI_paragraph_en": "The change from 121 to 122 units on 29 October 2026 corrected a roster-propagation omission for EXSCEL (NCT01144338), which was already present in the initial PubMed export and had a recorded inclusion decision. A pending exposure gate was resolved from its own article and registry safety groups documenting dosed participants in both arms. All 121 existing unit records and 3,388 assessment records were retained unchanged; EXSCEL was appended as one initial parallel unit with 28 pending/unknown positions. This was a technical admission correction under existing rules, not a new search hit, a split of an already admitted trial, or a new human eligibility vote. The exposure counts used for membership were not substituted for outcome-specific denominators, psychiatric counts or complete follow-up.",
